BUNDLED PROGRAMS
----------------

The Terminal screen runs the shell inside a terminal multiplexer when one can
be run. A build of Spagitty carries one for its platform, in the `multiplexer`
folder of its resources, with that program's licence texts beside it. These are
separate programs that Spagitty starts; none of their code is linked into it.
They are downloaded at build time by `tools/multiplexer.ts`, each from the
project that makes it, at a pinned version, and checked against a SHA-256.

  tmux 3.7c               ISC          macOS and Linux
    the tmux project's own static build (github.com/tmux/tmux-builds), which
    is linked against:
      libevent            BSD-3-Clause
      ncurses             MIT-style (X11)
      utf8proc            MIT
      musl                MIT          Linux only

  psmux 3.3.8             MIT          Windows
    github.com/psmux/psmux

On macOS and Linux the bundled tmux is used only when the system has no tmux
of version 3.2 or later.


